\subsection{Completed baseline and diagnostics}
The water CAS/B3LYP5 component discrepancy, six-record MP2/B3LYP5 comparison and water orbital-response controls reported above are completed findings, not outstanding proposed calculations. Their retained comparison prescriptions provide the baseline for additional work: identical solute geometry, MM sites and charges; water CAS(8e,6o) in fixed vacuum canonical RHF/cc-pVTZ orbitals, with zero-based orbital 0 (oxygen \(1s\)) inactive and orbitals 1--6 active; the full-basis B3LYP5/cc-pVTZ reproduction prescription described above; and all-electron MP2/cc-pVTZ. In the retained MP2 prescription the RHF reference relaxes at each scaled MM field; static interaction is the central total-energy derivative at zero field, evaluated with step \(h=0.0005\) and compared against \(h=0.001\) in the dimensionless parameter that scales the MM charges. The retained step comparison measures finite-difference sensitivity; it is not an absolute-error certificate. Static interaction is not an unrelaxed MP2-density contraction, and induction is the full-field minus vacuum energy minus that derivative. Preserve the consistent nuclear/MM contribution and report static and induced changes separately.\record{joint ledger entries 19 and 21; branch-3 Ada's V7 reference audit}

Keep the homogeneous-field response diagnostics separate from these embedded-component comparisons. The retained water diagnostics use cc-pVTZ and aug-cc-pVTZ to compare field-relaxed RHF and all-electron finite-field MP2 with CAS(8e,6o) under two orbital prescriptions: CASSCF optimises full-basis orbitals at each field; the fixed-optimised CASCI control instead holds zero-field CASSCF orbitals fixed at all fields. These diagnostics probe response lost by orbital restriction, but do not supply embedded static or induction energies. The zero-field energy-optimised fixed-orbital CASCI control also already failed to retain the relaxed water response; it is not the untested response-tailored alternative.

\subsection{Additional matched embedded comparison}
The additional prospective comparison is to test candidate response-tailored compressed spaces against augmented-basis DFT and correlated comparators for both static and induced components on identical retained geometry and MM inputs, with embedded charge spill-out assessed rather than inferred from gas-phase polarisability. Those candidate spaces and embedded tests have not been validated by the completed diagnostics. Field-specific orbital optimisation changes the actual determinants, so the prospective comparison must declare a common representation or account explicitly for orbital transport rather than identify determinants by unchanged bitstrings. The retained nonorthogonal-union and external-response alternatives remain conditional, with their classical preparation and transport costs unresolved. The finite-difference steps above belong to the retained MP2 comparator; the fixed-space CI static component uses the vacuum expectation already defined, not an imposed MP2 finite-difference prescription.\record{branch-1 entries 75 and 88; branch-3 entry 94; joint entry 7}

\subsection{Conditional selector decision}
The decision before another selector benchmark is whether a specified compressed Hamiltonian retains the embedded components of the better-converged physical comparators on identical inputs, informed separately by the basis and orbital-response diagnostics. Improved homogeneous-field response alone does not settle that comparison. Differences between methods do not certify which is accurate; the retained MP2 comparator is not exact, and neither an accuracy certificate nor a new numerical threshold or budget is supplied here. A persistent component deficit would direct further basis/orbital-response work before determinant-selection benchmarking; preservation of the relevant reference responses would support proceeding to a matched selector comparison within that tested model, not establish exact chemistry or hydration improvement. Disagreement between the physical comparators would leave reference adequacy unresolved. This states the conditional decisions, without selecting a new accuracy threshold or claiming a completed outcome.\record{joint ledger entries 7, 14, 19, 21, 32 and 64; branch-1 Ada's relaxed-control interpretation}
